# =============================================================================
# Kernel configuration shared by every variant
#
# The kernel recipe (distro/builder/os-recipes/linux.rhai) starts from
# x86_64_defconfig, applies this file and then the variant's own `kconfig`
# (only the options of its kernel line), sets CONFIG_LOCALVERSION from the
# variant id, and runs olddefconfig. Every CONFIG_ line here must survive
# olddefconfig on every variant's kernel line: a value the kernel drops (an
# unmet dependency, a renamed or removed symbol) fails the build. `=n` means
# "not built", which an unknown symbol also satisfies.
#
# - Snappy desktop: full preemption (switchable at boot), 1000Hz timer
# - Comprehensive hardware support (plug in anything, it works)
# - Live patching and checkpoint/restore, cgroups and namespaces for containers
# =============================================================================

# === PROCESSOR ===
